ategy to use?", "choice": "Hybrid: thin-slice first (Phase A), then parallel plugin development (Phase B), integration (Phase C), hardening (Phase D).", "rationale": "The thin-slice in Phase A validates the plugin lifecycle and core pipeline end-to-end before investing in parallel plugin work. This de-risks the plugin API design early. Parallel Phase B maximises throughput by allowing backlinks, tags, and search plugins to be developed concurrently. Phase C integration ensures all plugins work together before hardening.", "alternatives_considered": ["Fully sequential: lower risk but slower delivery.", "Fully parallel from start: higher risk of plugin API rework."], "what_would_change_this_decision": ["If only one developer is available, sequential phases would be more practical.", "If the plugin API is already proven (e.g., from a prior project), Phase A could be shortened."], "evidence_pointers": [{"artifact_ref": "branch_set_v1", "entity_id": null, "json_pointer": "/branches/1/milestone_strategy", "note": "Hybrid milestone strategy defined in branch", "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "Phase A (thin-slice): Build the core orchestrator (C8) with the file-collector plugin (C9) and Markdown parser plugin (C10)"}]}, {"id": "DEC3", "question": "When to resolve blocking questions Q1 (link syntax) and Q2 (tag format)?", "choice": "Resolve Q1 and Q2 before Phase A exits; canonical link model and tag specification are Phase A deliverables.", "rationale": "Plugin contracts for C11 (backlinks) and C12 (tags) depend on canonical link and tag models. Deferring these decisions would block Phase B parallel work and risk rework. K1 and K2 are both high-severity risks that must be mitigated early.", "alternatives_considered": ["Defer to Phase B: would block parallel plugin development.", "Resolve before Phase A starts: ideal but may not be feasible if stakeholder input is needed."], "what_would_change_this_decision": ["If stakeholders cannot provide input before 