ing validation."}], "hitl_triggers": ["Security-sensitive findings (e.g., XSS risk) lack a concrete mitigation.", "Performance/scale targets remain undefined while performance-sensitive features are being committed."]}, {"stage": "Review", "allowlisted_tools": ["artifact_read", "artifact_write"], "restrictions": [{"tool": "artifact_write", "rule": "write_required_outputs_only", "allowed_artifacts": ["review_findings", "audit_spine"], "notes": "Review must be able to write findings and update the audit spine."}, {"tool": "artifact_write", "rule": "no_untracked_decisions", "notes": "Any decision affecting link/tag spec, security posture, or hosting assumptions must be logged in review_findings."}, {"artifact_write": "canonical_allowed_only_for_declared_types", "notes": "Allow findings-only canonical artifacts (review_findings.json)."}], "hitl_triggers": ["Any acceptance of high/critical risks without explicit signoff rationale.", "Any change to blocking questions (Q1/Q2) without stakeholder approval."]}, {"stage": "Judge", "allowlisted_tools": ["artifact_read", "artifact_write"], "restrictions": [{"tool": "artifact_write", "rule": "decision_record_only", "allowed_artifacts": ["governance_decision", "risk_acceptance_log"], "notes": "Record accept/mitigate decisions only; no new features introduced."}], "hitl_triggers": ["Any critical risk remains unmitigated.", "Unresolved blocking questions remain (Q1 or Q2)."]}, {"stage": "Freeze", "allowlisted_tools": ["artifact_read", "artifact_write"], "restrictions": [{"tool": "artifact_write", "rule": "freeze_outputs_only", "allowed_artifacts": ["frozen_risk_register", "frozen_tool_policy"], "notes": "Freeze produces locked governance artifacts; edits require a new run."}], "hitl_triggers": ["Any attempt to modify frozen artifacts without a formal change request."]}]}, "hitl_policy": {"when_to_interrupt": ["Blocking specification decisions are required (Q1 internal link syntax; Q2 tag representation) and are not provided.", "Any proposal that violates the static-site constraint (requires a server/database at runtime).", "Any security-sensitive behavior is proposed (raw HTML passthrough, unsanitized rendering, unsafe URL schemes) without an explicit mitigation and reviewer approval.", "Any high/critical risk is proposed for acceptance rather than mitigation, or is accepted without explicit signoff rationale.", "Any ingestion behavior could read outside the intended directory (symlinks/path traversal) without explicit user confirmation.", "On repeated failures to pass critical path test cases.", "Before making significant architectural changes or adding new major dependencies.", "When a generated solution deviates from the defined project capsule requirements.", "Upon detection of a high-severity security vulnerability in code or dependencies."], "approval_roles": ["Product Owner", "Product Manager", "Tech Lead", "Engineering Lead", "Security Reviewer", "Security Analyst"]}}, "decision_log": [{"id": "DEC1", "question": "Which architecture option should be used for the MVP static-site generator?", "choice": "Choose O1: monolithic single-command CLI with an in-memory end-to-end pipeline (parse → compute links/tags/search → render).", "rationale": "O1 minimizes framework and API design overhead and provides the fastest path to an end-to-end, testable static site that meets core MUST requirements (ingest, render pages, backlinks, tags, client-side search).", "alternatives_considered": ["O2: plugin-based custom core (more extensible but higher upfront complexity).", "O3: Eleventy/SSG-based approach (faster via ecosystem, but adds dependency constraints/tooling and still needs custom backlink integration).", "O4: multi-tool pipeline with intermediate artifacts (modular but more orchestration complexity and I/O overhead)."], "what_would_change_this_decision": ["If rapid extensibility/themes/plugins becomes a near-term MUST (shift toward O2).", "If watch mode/incremental builds are required early and a mature SSG is acceptable (shift toward O3).", "If independent stage replacement becomes critical for multi-language tooling or team parallelism (shift toward O4)."], "evidence_pointers": [{"artifact_ref": "branch_set_v1", "entity_id": "O1", "json_pointer": "/inputs/branch/selected_arch_option_id", "note": "Branch selects O1 for speed and simplicity.", "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "selected_arch_option_id: O1"}, {"artifact_ref": "architecture_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "O1", "json_pointer": "/inputs/architecture/options/0/summary", "note": null, "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "Monolithic single-command CLI that runs an in-memory build pipeline end-to-end"}]}, {"id": "DEC2", "question": "How should delivery be staged to reduce risk while maintaining momentum?", "choice": "Use thin-slice milestones that each ship a usable static site increment, gated by mapped acceptance tests.", "rationale": "Thin slices enable early validation of core workflows (ingest → render → navigate) while containing complexity of backlinks/tags/search into later increments, aligning with acceptance-test gating and the branch’s speed-to-first-value posture.", "alternatives_considered": ["Big-bang build of all features before first usable output.", "Component-first build (finish parser/graph/search independently before rendering)."], "what_would_change_this_decision": ["If stakeholder needs require a complete feature set before any evaluation (switch to big-bang).", "If performance scale is extremely large and demands early architectural investment (front-load search/index and data model design)."], "evidence_pointers": [{"artifact_ref": "branch_set_v1", "entity_id": null, "json_pointer": "/inputs/branch/milestone_strategy", "note": null, "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "Each milestone delivers a shippable increment that can be tested against its acceptance tests"}, {"artifact_ref": "acceptance_canonical_v1", "entity_id": null, "json_pointer": "/inputs/acceptance_tests/acceptance_tests", "note": "Acceptance tests exist to gate each increment.", "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": null}]}, {"id": "DEC3", "question": "What is the policy for blocking specification questions (Q1 link syntax, Q2 tag representation)?", "choice": "Treat Q1 and Q2 as gating: resolve with HITL approval before implementing link/backlink or tag extraction behavior; encode results as explicit configuration/spec and fixtures.", "rationale": "Links/backlinks and tags are correctness-critical and ambiguous without a concrete spec; proceeding without resolution risks rework and incorrect navigation/tag completeness (K1, K2) and violates the project’s HITL triggers for blocking decisions.", "alternatives_considered": ["Attempt to auto-detect multiple link/tag formats without explicit specification.", "Implement only one assumed format without approval and revise later."], "what_would_change_this_decision": ["If stakeholders explicitly authorize a single default (e.g., GFM + standard Markdown links; frontmatter tags only) as the MVP scope.", "If a strong requirement emerges to support multiple dialects with auto-detection, along with acceptance tests that define expected behavior."], "evidence_pointers": [{"artifact_ref": "capsule_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "Q1", "json_pointer": "/inputs/project_capsule/open_questions/0", "note": "Blocking question for internal link syntax.", "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "What Markdown flavor and internal link syntax should be supported"}, {"artifact_ref": "capsule_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "Q2", "json_pointer": "/inputs/project_capsule/open_questions/1", "note": "Blocking question for tag representation.", "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "How are tags represented in the notes"}, {"artifact_ref": "risk_gov_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "K1", "json_pointer": "/inputs/risk_gov/risk_register/0/description", "note": null, "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "ambiguous or mixed internal link syntax ... causing broken navigation"}, {"artifact_ref": "risk_gov_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "K2", "json_pointer": "/inputs/risk_gov/risk_register/1/description", "note": null, "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "Tag extraction inconsistency due to unspecified or mixed tag formats"}]}, {"id": "DEC4", "question": "What default Markdown rendering security posture should be used to mitigate XSS (K3)?", "choice": "Default-deny: disable raw HTML in Markdown (or sanitize it), and block unsafe URL schemes (e.g., javascript:) in links/images; allow any relaxation only via explicit opt-in configuration with documentation.", "rationale": "The output is a browsable website; unsafe rendering can compromise readers. A strict default is aligned with K3 mitigation and the governance triggers around unsafe rendering.", "alternatives_considered": ["Allow raw HTML passthrough by default for maximum fidelity.", "Allow raw HTML but strip only known-bad tags/attributes without scheme checks."], "what_would_change_this_decision": ["If a stakeholder explicitly requires trusted raw HTML support and accepts the risk, with additional sanitization controls and tests.", "If a future plugin/theme system isolates trusted content and can enforce stronger CSP or sandboxing constraints."], "evidence_pointers": [{"artifact_ref": "risk_gov_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "K3", "json_pointer": "/inputs/risk_gov/risk_register/2/description", "note": null, "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "Client-side XSS or content injection vulnerabilities if Markdown/HTML is rendered unsafely"}, {"artifact_ref": "risk_gov_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "K3", "json_pointer": "/inputs/risk_gov/risk_register/2/mitigation/text", "note": null, "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "Disable raw HTML by default (or sanitize it) ... block unsafe URL schemes"}]}, {"id": "DEC5", "question": "How should ingestion be constrained to mitigate path traversal/unintended file inclusion (K9)?", "choice": "Constrain ingestion to the declared root input directory; do not follow symlinks by default; accept only .md files (and explicit static asset copies if needed) and reject any path that resolves outside the root.", "rationale": "Static generation must not accidentally leak local files. Symlinks and path traversal can cause inclusion of unintended content in the output site.", "alternatives_considered": ["Follow symlinks to support monorepo patterns and linked notes.", "Include any file type found under the root for convenience."], "what_would_change_this_decision": ["If a stakeholder explicitly requires symlink-following, with a safe allowlist and an inclusion manifest for review.", "If an asset pipeline is introduced with explicit include globs and manifest-based review."], "evidence_pointers": [{"artifact_ref": "risk_gov_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "K9", "json_pointer": "/inputs/risk_gov/risk_register/8/description", "note": null, "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "Path traversal or unintended file inclusion during ingestion (e.g., following symlinks)"}, {"artifact_ref": "risk_gov_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "K9", "json_pointer": "/inputs/risk_gov/risk_register/8/mitigation/text", "note": null, "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "Constrain ingestion to a declared root directory; default to not following symlinks"}]}, {"id": "DEC6", "question": "What is the MVP search approach under the static-site constraint (CNS1) and R5?", "choice": "Generate a build-time client-side search index artifact (e.g., JSON) and ship an in-browser JS search UI that loads and queries it with no server runtime.", "rationale": "This directly satisfies the static-site constraint and R5 while keeping the monolithic architecture simple. Scale concerns (K4) are addressed by adding a measurement step and deferring advanced scaling tactics until targets are known.", "alter