sm and stable URLs)."], "what_would_change_this_decision": ["If stakeholders require Obsidian-style title-based resolution even across folders, necessitating an explicit disambiguation/alias scheme.", "If a future feature requires URL schema changes (e.g., pretty URLs with configurable basePath and permalink patterns)."], "evidence_pointers": [{"artifact_ref": "requirements_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "R4", "json_pointer": "/inputs/requirements/requirements/3/text", "note": null, "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "stable URL derived deterministically from the note’s path/filename and/or a frontmatter-defined slug"}, {"artifact_ref": "risk_gov_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "K5", "json_pointer": "/inputs/risk_gov/risk_register/4/description", "note": null, "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "Slug/URL collisions ... cause pages to overwrite each other"}, {"artifact_ref": "risk_gov_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "K6", "json_pointer": "/inputs/risk_gov/risk_register/5/description", "note": null, "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "Non-deterministic builds ... produce noisy diffs and inconsistent site output"}]}], "supplemental_evaluations": [], "synthesis_warnings": [{"id": "W1", "severity": "high", "summary": "Branch acceptance strategy calls for adding a dedicated XSS acceptance test for K3 before M1 exit, but the canonical acceptance test list (AT1-AT13) contains no explicit XSS/security test. Adding a new acceptance test requires minting a new AT# (not allowed in this delta), so HITL/reroute is needed.", "routing_target": "Review/Security Reviewer", "evidence": [{"artifact_ref": "branch_set_v1", "entity_id": "K3", "json_pointer": "/inputs/branch/acceptance_strategy/notes", "note": null, "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": "A security-focused XSS acceptance test (covering K3) must be added before M1 exits."}, {"artifact_ref": "acceptance_canonical_v1", "entity_id": null, "json_pointer": "/inputs/acceptance