ow raw HTML or sanitize it; reject/neutralize unsafe URL schemes (e.g., javascript:) in links; require explicit opt-in config to allow trusted raw HTML with documented risk.", "rationale": "Directly mitigates critical XSS/content injection risk (K3) and aligns with the governance posture (sandboxed tooling; high HITL strictness).", "alternatives_considered": ["Allow raw HTML passthrough by default", "Allow raw HTML but warn only", "Strip all HTML always (may break legitimate content)"], "what_would_change_this_decision": ["If the user corpus requires trusted raw HTML, allow opt-in with clear warnings and a sanitizer allowlist policy.", "If a stricter environment is needed (public hosting with untrusted content), enforce sanitization with no opt-out."], "evidence_pointers": [{"artifact_ref": "risk_gov_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "K3", "json_pointer": "/risk_register/2", "note": "Critical XSS/content injection risk.", "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": null}, {"artifact_ref": "risk_gov_canonical_v1", "entity_id": null, "json_pointer": "/hitl_policy/when_to_interrupt/2", "note": "HITL trigger about unsafe rendering without mitigation.", "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": null}]}, {"id": "DEC7", "question": "How will client-side search indexing be designed initially under the plugin architecture?", "choice": "Start with a single build-time generated index artifact (e.g., JSON) consumed by the client runtime; keep the Search Index plugin interface capable of later sharding/chunking without changing the core orchestrator contract.", "rationale": "Meets R5 quickly while acknowledging K4 scale risk and preserving the ability to evolve toward sharded assets if needed, consistent with O2’s extensibility goal.", "alternatives_considered": ["Implement sharded/chunked indexing from day one", "Use an external SSG search toolchain (not applicable to custom core without added integration)", "Rely on browser-native search only (insufficient for R5/R