 may introduce breaking changes requiring maintenance", "Search indexing toolchain (e.g., Pagefind) may add CI/CD complexity on some platforms", "Wiki-link resolution plugin may not cover all desired dialects/edge cases without customization"]}, {"id": "O4", "summary": "Composable multi-tool pipeline: separate single-responsibility CLI tools (parser, backlink enricher, search indexer, renderer) communicate via intermediate on-disk artifacts (e.g., JSON), allowing independent development and replacement of stages while still producing a static site output.", "components": [{"id": "C23", "name": "Content Parser (CLI)", "responsibilities": ["Scan a directory of Markdown files", "Output a structured data file (e.g., notes.json) containing content, metadata, tags, and extracted forward links for every note"]}, {"id": "C24", "name": "Data Enricher (Backlinks) (CLI)", "responsibilities": ["Consume structured notes data from the parser", "Analyze the link graph to compute backlinks for each note", "Output an enriched structured data file including backlink information"]}, {"id": "C25", "name": "Search Indexer (CLI)", "responsibilities": ["Consume structured notes data from the parser (or enriched data if desired)", "Generate a static client-side search index artifact (e.g., JSON files)"]}, {"id": "C26", "name": "Site Renderer (CLI)", "responsibilities": ["Consume enriched structured data to generate final HTML pages using templates", "Copy generated pages, search index artifacts, and other static assets to the output directory"]}], "interfaces": [{"id": "IF23", "from": "C23", "to": "C24", "contract": "On-disk structured data file (e.g., notes.json) containing parsed note content/metadata and extracted forward links."}, {"id": "IF24", "from": "C23", "to": "C25", "contract": "On-disk structured data file (e.g., notes.json) containing parsed note content/metadata and extracted forward links."}, {"id": "IF25", "from": "C24", "to": "C26", "contract": "On-disk enriched data file (e.g., enriched-notes.json) containing backlink information per note."}, {"id": "IF26", "from": "C25", "to": "C26", "contract": "On-disk search index artifact(s) (e.g., search-index.json and related files) to be copied/embedded into the final site output."}], "tradeoffs": {"pros": ["High modularity: each stage can be developed, tested, and replaced independently", "Easier to mix technologies across stages (e.g., parser in one language, renderer in another)", "Clear intermediate artifact(s) can aid debugging and reproducibility"], "cons": ["More complex build orchestration for the end-user compared to a single command", "I/O overhead from writing/reading intermediate files can reduce performance", "Intermediate schema/versioning must be maintained carefully across tools"]}, "risks": ["User experience may suffer if orchestration is cumbersome (multiple commands, ordering, cleanup)", "Intermediate JSON/schema changes require coordinated updates across multiple tools", "Disk usage can increase due to large intermediate artifacts on big note sets"]}], "chosen": {"option_id": "O1", "rationale": "The monolithic single-command CLI (O1) minimises upfront design overhead, avoids plugin-API or SSG-dependency risks, and delivers the fastest path to a working end-to-end prototype. All build stages run in-memory in a single process, simplifying debugging and deployment. Thin-slice milestones let each core goal (G1–G5) be validated incrementally. The trade-off is reduced long-term extensibility compared to O2 or O3, but this is acceptable given the project's scope and the explicit deferral of COULD requirements to post-MVP.", "high_level_dataflow": "User invokes CLI (C1) with input/output paths → C2 recursively discovers .md files, parses Markdown to AST, extracts frontmatter/tags/links → C3 builds forward-link graph and computes backlinks → C4 aggregates tags into per-tag indexes → C5 builds client-side search index → C6 renders HTML pages (injecting backlinks, tags, navigation) 