inks resolve and are clickable.", "AT9 passes: 100% of expected backlinks appear on target pages.", "Broken-link warnings emitted with source file/line (K1 mitigation).", "Backlink correctness validated against deterministic fixture dataset."], "depends_on": ["M1"]}, {"id": "M3", "name": "Tag Extraction & Navigation", "deliverables": [{"id": "DL11", "text": "Tag extraction logic in C2 supporting the resolved tag convention from Q2 (frontmatter and/or inline)."}, {"id": "DL12", "text": "Tag index builder (C4) producing per-tag note lists."}, {"id": "DL13", "text": "Per-tag navigation pages and tag index page rendered by C6."}, {"id": "DL14", "text": "Fixture-based test dataset validating 100% tag completeness (R20)."}, {"id": "DL15", "text": "Acceptance tests AT6, AT7 passing."}], "exit_criteria": ["AT6 passes: 100% of tagged notes appear under correct tag pages.", "AT7 passes: each tag has a navigable listing with working links.", "Tag completeness validated against deterministic fixture dataset."], "depends_on": ["M1"]}, {"id": "M4", "name": "Client-Side Search", "deliverables": [{"id": "DL16", "text": "Search index generator (C5) producing a client-side full-text index artifact at build time."}, {"id": "DL17", "text": "Client-side search UI (C7) loading the index and rendering results with title, snippet, and navigation."}, {"id": "DL18", "text": "Search quality benchmark against representative query set (R19)."}, {"id": "DL19", "text": "Search index size/performance benchmark for 100+ note dataset (K4)."}, {"id": "DL20", "text": "Acceptance tests AT5, AT12 passing."}], "exit_criteria": ["AT5 passes: search operates fully client-side without network.", "AT12 passes: ≥90% of representative queries return expected note in top 10.", "Search index size and query latency benchmarked and documented (K4)."], "depends_on": ["M1"]}, {"id": "M5", "name": "Polish & Optional Features", "deliverables": [{"id": "DL21", "text": "Clear error reporting for invalid Markdown, unresolvable links, and tag parsing failures with file paths and line numbers (R12)."}, {"id": "DL22", "text": "Cross-browser validation across Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge (R13)."}, {"id": "DL23", "text": "Watch mode for incremental regeneration (R25)."}, {"id": "DL24", "text": "Per-note table of contents generation (R24)."}, {"id": "DL25", "text": "Optional features scoped and implemented as approved: graph view (R26), theming (R27), advanced search (R28), nested tags (R29)."}, {"id": "DL26", "text": "Acceptance tests AT10, AT11 passing."}], "exit_criteria": ["AT10 passes: CLI build completes offline with input/output paths.", "AT11 passes: core features work without runtime errors in all target browsers.", "R12 error reporting verified on intentionally malformed inputs.", "Watch mode tested for edit/rename/delete scenarios (K14 mitigation).", "COULD features only implemented with explicit product approval (K20)."], "depends_on": ["M2", "M3", "M4"]}], "risk_register": [{"id": "K1", "severity": "high", "description": "Link/backlink resolution errors due to ambiguous or mixed internal link syntax (e.g., Markdown links vs. WikiLinks), causing broken navigation and incorrect backlink lists (blocking Q1).", "mitigation": {"text": "Resolve and document the supported internal link syntax (Q1). Implement a single canonical internal link model (normalized target IDs) with deterministic resolution rules. Add fixture-based tests for edge cases (relative paths, anchors, URL-encoding, renamed files). Emit build warnings for unresolved links including source locations.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K2", "severity": "high", "description": "Tag extraction inconsistency due to unspecified or mixed tag formats (frontmatter vs inline tags; nested tags), leading to missing/incorrect tag pages and filtering (blocking Q2).", "mitigation": {"text": "Resolve and document the tag specification (Q2). Implement a deterministic tag parser with explicit precedence rules and validation (report invalid tokens). Produce a build-time summary/tag inventory and add tests for the chosen formats (frontmatter, inline, optional nested).", "owner": "Product/Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K3", "severity": "critical", "description": "Client-side XSS or content injection vulnerabilities if Markdown/HTML is rendered unsafely (e.g., raw HTML passthrough, unsafe link protocols), compromising readers of the static site.", "mitigation": {"text": "Disable raw HTML by default (or sanitize it) in the renderer; block unsafe URL schemes (e.g., javascript:) and enforce safe attributes. Add security tests with known XSS payloads. If allowing trusted raw HTML, require explicit opt-in configuration and document the risk.", "owner": "Security/Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K4", "severity": "high", "description": "Client-side search index size/quality/performance may degrade at scale (large JS payload, slow queries, long build time), causing poor UX or crashes (related to Q3/SM7).", "mitigation": {"text": "Define expected scale and performance targets (Q3). Choose an index approach suitable for in-browser search; apply index-size controls (tokenization choices, compression, lazy loading/chunking where applicable). Add benchmark fixtures and CI performance budgets; validate search quality targets against representative queries.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K5", "severity": "medium", "description": "Slug/URL collisions (e.g., same filename in different folders, case-insensitive filesystems) cause pages to overwrite each other or links to resolve unpredictably.", "mitigation": {"text": "Define a deterministic slug strategy (include path segments and/or stable hashing). Detect collisions during build and fail with actionable errors unless an explicit override map is provided.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K6", "severity": "high", "description": "Non-deterministic builds (ordering differences, locale/time-dependent formatting, unpinned dependencies) produce noisy diffs and inconsistent site output across machines/CI.", "mitigation": {"text": "Enforce determinism: stable sorting of inputs, fixed locale/timezone handling, content-hash-based asset naming, and pinned dependency versions/lockfiles. Add a reproducibility check comparing outputs across two clean runs.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K7", "severity": "high", "description": "Markdown flavor/extension mismatch or unsupported/non-standard syntax yields rendering differences, broken formatting, or build failures relative to user expectations.", "mitigation": {"text": "Select and document a supported Markdown flavor and extensions (e.g., CommonMark baseline with explicit GFM extensions if supported). Add a conformance test pack with representative notes, robust error handling, and a strict mode that flags unsupported syntax.", "owner": "Product/Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K8", "severity": "medium", "description": "File encoding and Unicode handling issues (non-UTF8, BOM, mixed line endings) cause build failures or corrupted output text/search results.", "mitigation": {"text": "Assume UTF-8 by default but detect/handle BOM and common encodings where feasible. Normalize line endings internally. Emit clear diagnostics identifying offending files and provide a preflight validation command.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K9", "severity": "high", "description": "Path traversal or unintended file inclusion during ingestion (e.g., following symlinks, reading outside the intended directory) could leak local files into the generated site.", "mitigation": {"text": "Constrain ingestion to a declared root directory; default to not following symlinks; maintain an allowlist of file 