t and a compatibility policy.", "owner": "Product/Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K17", "severity": "medium", "description": "Information disclosure via generated artifacts (e.g., including private notes, embedding absolute filesystem paths in HTML/JS/search index).", "mitigation": {"text": "Support exclude patterns (globs) and a 'private' frontmatter flag. Ensure generated output never includes absolute source paths (use relative identifiers only). Emit a build manifest listing included sources for review.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K18", "severity": "high", "description": "Poorly managed third-party dependencies (e.g., Markdown parser, search indexer/SSG plugins) may introduce breaking changes or security vulnerabilities that destabilize the tool.", "mitigation": {"text": "Pin dependency versions and use a lockfile. Establish a dependency update/vetting process including automated vulnerability scanning and regression testing before upgrades.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K19", "severity": "medium", "description": "A complex installation process or system-specific dependencies for the CLI tool can create a high barrier to entry for users.", "mitigation": {"text": "Target a simple installation path (e.g., a single package manager). Document prerequisites clearly; minimize system-specific dependencies; consider producing distributable bundles where feasible.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K20", "severity": "low", "description": "Scope creep from undefined secondary features (e.g., graph views, themes) could divert resources from core goals and delay delivery.", "mitigation": {"text": "Prioritize core features for MVP; defer optional features until after MVP and track them as distinct work items with explicit approval before implementation.", "owner": "Product", "status": "planned"}, "acceptanc