tag navigation pages (R7, R8, R20). Milestone 4 delivers client-side search index generation and search UI (R5, R19). Milestone 5 polishes the tool with error reporting (R12), cross-browser validation (R13), watch mode (R25), and optional features (R24, R26–R29). Blocking questions Q1 (link syntax) and Q2 (tag format) must be resolved before coding begins. XSS mitigation (K3) is enforced from day one by disabling raw HTML and blocking unsafe URL schemes. High HITL strictness ensures stakeholder sign-off at each milestone gate. This branch optimises for speed-to-first-value and simplicity at the cost of long-term extensibility.", "requirements": [{"id": "R1", "priority": "MUST", "text": "The system MUST accept a user-specified folder (or repository working directory) as input and recursively discover Markdown (.md) files to form the notes corpus.", "rationale": "Core workflow requires ingesting a directory of Markdown notes to generate the site."}, {"id": "R2", "priority": "MUST", "text": "The system MUST generate a static website output consisting only of static files (HTML/CSS/JS/assets) that can be hosted or viewed without any required server-side runtime for browsing, search, tags, or backlinks.", "rationale": "Static-only output is a hard constraint and aligns with the non-goal of requiring a backend at runtime."}, {"id": "R3", "priority": "MUST", "text": "The system MUST parse and render each input Markdown file into a corresponding static HTML page while preserving Markdown formatting and structure (e.g., headings, lists, code blocks, emphasis, links; and commonly used elements such as images and tables when supported by the selected flavor).", "rationale": "Readable output requires faithful Markdown-to-HTML rendering consistent with the project’s chosen Markdown flavor."}, {"id": "R4", "priority": "MUST", "text": "The system MUST produce one distinct, navigable page per input note, with each page having a stable URL derived deterministically from the note’s path/filename and/or a frontmatter-defined slug.", "rationale": "Stable per-note pages are necessary for browsing, deep linking, and consistent forward links/backlinks."}, {"id": "R5", "priority": "MUST", "text": "The system MUST build a client-side full-text search index at generation time and provide an in-browser search UI that searches across all note contents (and titles where available) without a server.", "rationale": "Full-text search is a primary goal and must operate entirely in the browser to satisfy the static-site constraint."}, {"id": "R6", "priority": "SHOULD", "text": "The search UI SHOULD display a results list including each matching note’s title (or filename) and a snippet and/or highlighted match context; selecting a result SHOULD navigate to the corresponding note page.", "rationale": "Improves search usability and supports practical discoverability at scale."}, {"id": "R7", "priority": "MUST", "text": "The system MUST extract tags from notes using a specified, consistent convention and expose tag-based browsing/filtering in the generated site.", "rationale": "Tags are a stated goal; consistent parsing is required for reliable tag navigation."}, {"id": "R8", "priority": "MUST", "text": "The generated site MUST provide a per-tag navigation experience such that each tag has a listing of all notes containing that tag (e.g., tag pages and/or tag filters).", "rationale": "Makes tags actionable for navigation and supports the tag browsing goal."}, {"id": "R9", "priority": "MUST", "text": "The system MUST detect forward links between notes based on a specified internal link syntax and render those links as clickable navigational elements in output pages.", "rationale": "Forward link rendering is required for cross-note navigation and is prerequisite for backlink computation."}, {"id": "R10", "priority": "MUST", "text": "The system MUST compute backlinks for each note by analyzing the corpus link graph and render a backlinks section on each note page listing all notes that link to it.", "rationale": "Backlinks are a core requirement and a key differentiator for navigability."}, {"id": "R11", "priority": "MUST", "text": "The system MUST be invocable as an offline build step via a command-line interface (CLI) that accepts at minimum an input directory path and an output directory path, and core generation MUST NOT require network access.", "rationale": "Aligns with the intended workflow (local build) and supports static hosting without backend dependencies."}, {"id": "R12", "priority": "SHOULD", "text": "The build process SHOULD provide clear error reporting for invalid Markdown, unresolvable internal links, or tag parsing failures, including file paths and line/position where applicable.", "rationale": "Improves maintainability and reduces friction when scaling to large note corpora."}, {"id": "R13", "priority": "MUST", "text": "The generated site MUST function in modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge) with core features (navigation, search, tag browsing, backlinks) working without runtime errors.", "rationale": "Cross-browser functionality is an explicit success metric for the generated static site."}, {"id": "R14", "priority": "SHOULD", "text": "The system SHOULD support configuration of the Markdown flavor, internal link syntax, and tag conventions used for parsing and site generation.", "rationale": "Key conventions are open questions; configurability helps avoid overpromising universal compatibility while allowing explicit selection."}, {"id": "R15", "priority": "SHOULD", "text": "The system SHOULD support CommonMark as a baseline Markdown flavor and SHOULD additionally support GitHub-Flavored Markdown (GFM) extensions such as tables, task lists, and strikethrough, with the exact flavor finalized based on the project’s selected conventions.", "rationale": "Establishes a concrete baseline for Markdown processing while allowing finalization per the project’s link/flavor decisions."}, {"id": "R16", "priority": "SHOULD", "text": "The system SHOULD support wiki-link style inter-note links (e.g., [[Note Title]]) in addition to standard Markdown links, with the exact syntax finalized based on the project’s chosen link convention.", "rationale": "Wiki-links are common in note-taking tools and broaden compatibility, but exact syntax is an open question."}, {"id": "R17", "priority": "SHOULD", "text": "The system SHOULD include a site-wide navigation structure with at minimum (a) an index/home page listing all notes and (b) a tag index page listing all tags.", "rationale": "Improves discoverability and makes the generated site easier to browse."}, {"id": "R18", "priority": "SHOULD", "text": "The system SHOULD support extracting tags from both YAML frontmatter and inline #tag syntax, with an option to configure which sources are used, aligned with the project’s selected tag convention.", "rationale": "Supports compatibility with different tagging styles; details depend on the project’s tag representation decision."}, {"id": "R19", "priority": "MUST", "text": "Search results MUST meet the defined search quality target: at least 90% of predefined representative queries return the expected note within the top 10 results.", "rationale": "Codifies the stated search success metric as a verifiable requirement."}, {"id": "R20", "priority": "MUST", "text": "Tag navigation MUST be complete: 100% of notes containing tags in the dataset MUST appear under their corresponding tag pages or filters in the generated site.", "rationale": "Codifies the tag correctness success metric as a verifiable requirement."}, {"id": "R21", "priority": "MUST", "text": "Backlink rendering MUST be correct: for a test set of interlinked notes, 100% of expected backlinks MUST appear on their target note pages.", "rationale": "Codifies the backlink correctness success metric as a verifiable requirement."}, {"id": "R22", "priority": "MUST", "text": "The build process MUST complete without errors on a representative notes folder and produce a valid set of static files.", "rationale": "Codifies the baseline build success metric required before other features can be evaluated."}, {"id": "R23", "priority": "SHOULD", "text": "On a representative dataset of 100+ notes, the system SHOULD meet agreed performance targets for generation time and in-browser search responsiveness; these targets SHOULD be defined/documented based on expected scale (e.g., search results within 500ms).", "rationale": "Performance requirements depend on scale, which is not yet fully specified; this ensures explicit targets and validation."}, {"id": "R24", "priority": "SHOULD", "text": "The system SHOULD generate a table of contents (outline) for each note page based on its heading structure.", "rationale": "Improves within-note navigation, especially for long notes."}, {"id": "R25", "priority": "SHOULD", "text": "The CLI SHOULD provide a watch mode that monitors the input directory for changes and incrementally regenerates affected pages.", "rationale": "Improves the authoring workflow during active note editing and site preview."}, {"id": "R26", "priority": "COULD", "text": "The generated site COULD include an interactive graph view visualizing link relationships between notes.", "rationale": "Optional discovery feature; not required for core generation, tags, search, and backlinks."}, {"id": "R27", "priority": "COULD", "text": "The system COULD support theming or customizable styling of the generated site via user-provided CSS or theme configuration.", "rationale": "Optional customization feature; not required for core functionality."}, {"id": "R28", "priority": "COULD", "text": "Search COULD support advanced features such as fuzzy matching, tag-based filtering, result highlighting, and sorting by relevance.", "rationale": "Optional enhancements to search experience beyond basic full-text search."}, {"id": "R29", "priority": "COULD", "text": "The system COULD support nested/hierarchical tags (e.g., #parent/child) and reflect the hierarchy in tag navigation.", "rationale": "Optional capability for complex tag taxonomies; not required for baseline tag browsing."}], "acceptance_tests": [{"id": "AT1", "maps_to_requirements": ["R1"], "type": "system", "procedure": "Create a test input directory with nested subfolders containing .md files and non-.md files. Run the CLI build specifying the root input directory and an output directory. Inspect the discovered notes list (build log or generated site pages) to confirm recursive discovery.", "pass_criteria": "All .md files in all subfolders are included as notes; non-.md files are excluded."}, {"id": "AT2", "maps_to_requirements": ["R2"], "type": "system", "procedure": "Run the build on a representative notes folder. Inspect the output directory contents and attempt to open the site via a local static file server (or static hosting).", "pass_criteria": "Build completes successfully; output contains only static assets (HTML/CSS/JS/media); site functions without any server-side runtime for browsing, search, tags, or backlinks."}, {"id": "AT3", "maps_to_requirements": ["R3"], "type": "human_eval", "procedure": "Prepare notes covering headings, lists, code blocks, blockquotes, links, images, and tables per the selected Markdown flavor. Build the site and visually compare rendered HTML output to expected formatting.", "pass_criteria": "All tested Markdown elements render correctly and preserve structure and formatting."}, {"id": "AT4", "maps_to_requirements": ["R4"], "type": "system", "procedure": "Create notes with known filenames/paths and optional frontmatter slugs. Build the site and record the generated URLs for each note. Rebuild without changes and compare URLs.", "pass_criteria": "Each note has a distinct page; URLs are deterministically derived from path/filename or frontmatter slug and remain stable across rebuilds."}, {"id": "AT5", "maps_to_requirements": ["R5"], "type": "system", "procedure": "Build the site and verify that a search index artifact is generated. Open the site in a browser with network disabled and perform searches via the UI.", "pass_criteria": "Search operates fully client-side without network access; search returns results across note contents/titles."}, {"id": "AT6", "maps_to_requirements": ["R7", "R20"], "type": "system", "procedure": "Create a dataset with tagged and untagged notes using the specified tag convention. Build the site and navigate tag pages/filters. Count notes per tag and compare with source data.", "pass_criteria": "All tagged notes appear under each corresponding tag; untagged notes are not listed; 100% of notes with tags are included under the correct tag pages/filters."}, {"id": "AT7", "maps_to_requirements": ["R8"], "type": "system", "procedure": "Build a dataset with multiple tags across notes. Build the site and navigate to each tag’s listing page or filter UI.", "pass_criteria": "Each tag has a navigable listing showing all notes containing that tag, with working links to note pages."}, {"id": "AT8", "maps_to_requirements": ["R9"], "type": "system", "procedure": "Create notes with internal forward links using the specified link syntax. Build the site and click each internal link in rendered pages.", "pass_criteria": "All internal links resolve to the correct target note pages and are rendered as clickable elements."}, {"id": "AT9", "maps_to_requirements": ["R10", "R21"], "type": "system", "procedure": "Create a known link graph (e.g., A→B, C→B, B→D). Build the site and inspect backlinks sections on each note page.", "pass_criteria": "Each note’s backlinks list includes all and only notes that link to it; for the test set, 100% of expected backlinks appear."}, {"id": "AT10", "maps_to_requirements": ["R11"], "type": "system", "procedure": "Run the CLI build specifying input and output directories while offline (no network).", "pass_criteria": "CLI accepts input/output paths; build completes without network access and produces the static site output."}, {"id": "AT11", "maps_to_requirements": ["R13"], "type": "human_eval", "procedure": "Open the generated site in latest Chrome, Firefox, Safari, and Edge. Test navigation, search, tag browsing, and backlinks in each browser.", "pass_criteria": "Core features function without runtime errors in all listed browsers."}, {"id": "AT12", "maps_to_requirements": ["R19"], "type": "metric", "procedure": "Define a representative query set with expected target notes. Build the site and execute each query in the search UI, recording the top 10 results.", "pass_criteria": "At least 90% of queries return the expected note within the top 10 results."}, {"id": "AT13", "maps_to_requirements": ["R22"], "type": "system", "procedure": "Run the build on a representative notes folder and monitor for errors. Verify output directory contains generated static files.", "pass_criteria": "Build completes without errors and produces a valid set of static files."}], "architecture": {"options": [{"id": "O1", "summary": "Monolithic single-command CLI that runs an in-memory build pipeline end-to-end: read Markdown notes, extract metadata/tags/links, compute backlinks, build a client-side search index, and render a complete static HTML/CSS/JS site in one execution.", "components": [{"id": "C1", "name": "CLI Entry Point / Orchestrator", "responsibilities": ["Parse command-line arguments (input folder, output folder, config file path)", "Orchestrate the build pipeline stages in sequence in a single run", "Report build progress and errors to stdout/stderr"]}, {"id": "C2", "name": "Markdown Parser & Metadata Extractor", "responsibilities": ["Read all .md files from the input directory tree", "Parse YAML frontmatter to extract tags and metadata", "Parse Markdown into an AST and/or HTML-ready representation", "Detect and normalize internal links (standard Markdown links and optional wiki-links)"]}, {"id": "C3", "name": "Graph (Links/Backlinks) Engine", "responsibilities": ["Build a forward-link graph from parsed internal links", "Compute backlinks for every note from the inverse graph", "Resolve link targets to output URLs", "Report broken/unresolvable links as warnings"]}, {"id": "C4", "name": "Tag Index Builder", "responsibilities": ["Aggregate tags across all notes", "Generate per-tag note lists", "Produce a tag index structure for tag browsing pages"]}, {"id": "C5", "name": "Search Index Generator", "responsibilities": ["Build a client-side full-text search index from note titles/content/tags at build time", "Serialize the index to a JSON (or equivalent) file included in the static output", "Apply basic index-size controls (e.g., stemming/stop words) as needed"]}, {"id": "C6", "name": "HTML Renderer / Templating", "responsibilities": ["Convert Markdown/AST to HTML", "Inject backlinks, tag lists, and navigation into page templates", "Render tag index pages, home page, and search page", "Copy static assets (CSS, JS, images) to the output directory"]}, {"id": "C7", "name": "Client-Side Search UI", "responsibilities": ["Load the pre-built search index in the browser", "Provide a search input with results rendering", "Optionally highlight matched terms in result snippets"]}], "interfaces": [{"id": "IF1", "from": "C1", "to": "C2", "contract": "Pass input directory path and config (Markdown flavor, link/tag syntax options) to the parser/extractor."}, {"id": "IF2", "from": "C2", "to": "C3", "contract": "Emit in-memory note records including slugs/titles/metadata and extracted forward links for link graph + backlink computation."}, {"id": "IF3", "from": "C2", "to": "C4", "contract": "Provide extracted tags per note (from frontmatter and/or inline tag syntax) for aggregation and tag page generation."}, {"id": "IF4", "from": "C2", "to": "C5", "contract": "Provide per-note indexable fields (slug, title, plain text content, tags) to build the search index artifact."}, {"id": "IF5", "from": "C3", "to": "C6", "contract": "Provide backlinks per note (e.g., Map<slug, BacklinkEntry[]>) for rendering on note pages."}, {"id": "IF6", "from": "C4", "to": "C6", "contract": "Provide tag index (e.g., Map<tag, slug[]>) for rendering tag pages and per-note tag navigation."}, {"id": "IF7", "from": "C5", "to": "C6", "contract": "Output a serialized search index file into the output assets and return its relative path for inclusion in the rendered site."}, {"id": "IF8", "from": "C6", "to": "C7", "contract": "Rendered search page references the search index asset and client-side JS bundle via static <script>/<link> tags."}], "tradeoffs": {"pros": ["Simple single-process build; easy to reason about and debug", "Simple user experience: one command generates the whole site", "Potentially fast for small-to-medium note sets due to in-memory stage handoff", "Straightforward deployment: run CLI, upload output folder"], "cons": ["Monolithic codebase can become harder to extend (themes, graph view, alternative search backends)", "Less flexibility to swap individual parts without code changes", "Often implies full rebuild on any change unless incremental build is explicitly implemented", "Client-side search index size can grow and impact first-load performance for large note sets"]}, "risks": ["Search index asset may become too large for very large note sets, degrading initial load time", "Memory usage can grow substantially at very large scale (e.g., many thousands of notes) due to in-memory representations", "Wiki-link and tag syntax ambiguity can cause incorrect extraction/resolution without a clear specification", "Single-threaded sequential build may become slow on very large repositories"]}, {"id": "O2", "summary": "Custom plugin-based static site generator core with a formal build lifecycle and plugin API; each concern (file collection, Markdown parsing, backlinks, tags, search, theming) is a plugin, enabling swapping/extending behavior without modifying the core.", "components": [{"id": "C8", "name": "Core Orchestrator & Plugin Host", "responsibilities": ["Load configuration and discover/register plugins", "Define and execute build lifecycle hooks (init, collectFiles, transform, resolve, render, finalize)", "Manage shared build context (note registry, site metadata, output paths)"]}, {"id": "C9", "name": "File Collector Plugin", "responsibilities": ["Recursively scan input directory for Markdown files", "Emit file metadata into the shared note registry", "Support configurable file include/exclude patterns"]}, {"id": "C10", "name": "Markdown Parser Plugin", "responsibilities": ["Parse each Markdown file into an AST (or equivalent)", "Extract YAML frontmatter", "Normalize internal link references into a canonical format"]}, {"id": "C11", "name": "Backlink Resolver Plugin", "responsibilities": ["Build forward-link and backlink graphs from parsed link data", "Attach backlink metadata to each note in the shared registry"]}, {"id": "C12", "name": "Tag Aggregator Plugin", "responsibilities": ["Collect tags from frontmatter and/or inline tag syntax", "Build tag-to-notes index", "Register tag index pages for rendering"]}, {"id": "C13", "name": "Search Index Plugin", "responsibilities": ["Build a client-side search index and write index artifacts to the output directory", "Optionally support chunked/sharded index artifacts for larger sites"]}, {"id": "C14", "name": "Theme / Renderer Plugin", "responsibilities": ["Provide HTML templates and CSS/JS assets", "Render note pages and index/tag/search pages using the shared build context", "Support theme switching via configuration"]}, {"id": "C15", "name": "Client-Side Runtime", "responsibilities": ["Load and query the generated search index assets in the browser", "Render interactive search results and navigation UI elements", "Provide tag filter UI and backlink navigation"]}], "interfaces": [{"id": "IF9", "from": "C8", "to": "C9", "contract": "Hook: collectFiles(context) → context.noteRegistry populated with entries (filePath, slug)."}, {"id": "IF10", "from": "C8", "to": "C10", "contract": "Hook: transform(context) → each note enriched with (ast, frontmatter, rawLinks[])."}, {"id": "IF11", "from": "C8", "to": "C11", "contract": "Hook: resolve(context) → backlink map attached to context and/or notes."}, {"id": "IF12", "from": "C8", "to": "C12", "contract": "Hook: resolve(context) → tag index attached to context and tag pages registered for render."}, {"id": "IF13", "from": "C8", "to": "C13", "contract": "Hook: finalize(context) → search index artifacts written to output directory (optionally sharded)."}, {"id": "IF14", "from": "C8", "to": "C14", "contract": "Hook: render(context) → HTML files and static theme assets written to output directory using context data."}, {"id": "IF15", "from": "C14", "to": "C15", "contract": "Rendered pages reference client-side JS bundle and search index assets via relative static paths."}], "tradeoffs": {"pros": ["Highly extensible: new features can be added as plugins without changing the core", "Clean separation of concerns, improving testability and maintainability", "Themes and search backends can be swapped via plugin selection/configuration", "Can evolve toward large-site needs (e.g., sharded search indexes) within a consistent lifecycle"], "cons": ["More upfront design and implementation effort (plugin API, hook semantics, shared context schema)", "Plugin ordering and inter-plugin dependencies add complexity", "Debugging cross-plugin issues can be harder than a monolith", "Over-engineering risk for a small-scope initial release"]}, "risks": ["Plugin API may need multiple iterations to stabilize, delaying initial delivery", "Poorly specified plugin contracts can lead to brittle plugins and breaking changes", "Performance overhead or complexity from hook dispatch and large shared context objects may emerge at scale"]}, {"id": "O3", "summary": "Use an existing static site generator (SSG), specifically Eleventy/11ty, as the build engine; implement backlinks, tags, and search as Eleventy plugins/config, leveraging its templating, collections/data model, and watch/incremental build capabilities (with Pagefind for scalable client-side search).", "components": [{"id": "C16", "name": "Eleventy (11ty) Core Engine", "responsibilities": ["Handle file discovery, templating, and static output generation", "Provide data cascade and collections APIs for structured content data", "Support watch mode and incremental rebuilds"]}, {"id": "C17", "name": "Markdown Processing Configuration", "responsibilities": ["Configure Markdown library/flavor and parsing options", "Add wiki-link syntax support via Markdown plugin (if required)", "Extract frontmatter into Eleventy’s data model"]}, {"id": "C18", "name": "Backlink Data Plugin (Eleventy Plugin)", "responsibilities": ["Scan collections/content for internal links", "Compute backlinks and inject backlink data into each note’s template data"]}, {"id": "C19", "name": "Tag Collections & Tag Pages", "responsibilities": ["Use Eleventy’s tags/collections mechanisms to aggregate tags", "Generate per-tag index pages (e.g., via pagination templates)", "Provide tag lists/tag cloud data to templates"]}, {"id": "C20", "name": "Search Index Build Step (Pagefind or equivalent)", "responsibilities": ["Generate a client-side full-text search index during/after the Eleventy build", "Index the rendered HTML output for accurate search over final content", "Write search assets into the output directory"]}, {"id": "C21", "name": "Theme / Layout Templates", "responsibilities": ["Provide templates for note pages, tag pages, home, and search", "Include CSS and any client-side JS needed for navigation/backlinks/search integration", "Render backlink sections and tag links within templates"]}, {"id": "C22", "name": "Client-Side Search UI (Pagefind UI or custom)", "responsibilities": ["Load chunked search index assets on demand", "Provide interactive search UI with highlighting", "Operate entirely client-side in the static site"]}], "interfaces": [{"id": "IF16", "from": "C16", "to": "C17", "contract": "Eleventy config registers Markdown processing (including wiki-link plugin if needed); .md files are processed through this configuration."}, {"id": "IF17", "from": "C16", "to": "C18", "contract": "Eleventy plugin hook/collection step receives all notes/collection items and can compute backlinks to inject into template data."}, {"id": "IF18", "from": "C18", "to": "C21", "contract": "Each note’s data object includes backlinks[] (e.g., {slug, title, excerpt/context}) available to templates."}, {"id": "IF19", "from": "C16", "to": "C19", "contract": "Tags/collections are populated from frontmatter tags (and/or derived tags) and made available to templates and pagination."}, {"id": "IF20", "from": "C16", "to": "C20", "contract": "AfterBuild (or equivalent) triggers search indexing against the built output directory."}, {"id": "IF21", "from": "C20", "to": "C22", "contract": "Search build step outputs static (often chunked) search assets; the search page includes references to these assets and UI JS."}, {"id": "IF22", "from": "C21", "to": "C16", "contract": "Templates are registered/configured in Eleventy and used to produce final static output files."}], "tradeoffs": {"pros": ["Reduces custom code by leveraging a mature SSG for file handling and templating", "Watch mode and incremental builds available out of the box", "Pagefind-style search produces chunked indexes that scale better to thousands of pages", "Access to ecosystem of plugins/themes and community support"], "cons": ["Constrained by the chosen SSG’s conventions, APIs, and upgrade cycle", "Backlink computation still requires custom integration with the SSG data model", "Less control over build pipeline internals than a fully custom generator", "Additional dependencies (SSG + plugins), and potentially a non-JS binary for search indexing"]}, "risks": ["SSG plugin/data model limitations may force workarounds for specific features", "Upgrades to the SSG or plugin APIs may introduce breaking changes requiring maintenance", "Search indexing toolchain (e.g., Pagefind) may add CI/CD complexity on some platforms", "Wiki-link resolution plugin may not cover all desired dialects/edge cases without customization"]}, {"id": "O4", "summary": "Composable multi-tool pipeline: separate single-responsibility CLI tools (parser, backlink enricher, search indexer, renderer) communicate via intermediate on-disk artifacts (e.g., JSON), allowing independent development and replacement of stages while still producing a static site output.", "components": [{"id": "C23", "name": "Content Parser (CLI)", "responsibilities": ["Scan a directory of Markdown files", "Output a structured data file (e.g., notes.json) containing content, metadata, tags, and extracted forward links for every note"]}, {"id": "C24", "name": "Data Enricher (Backlinks) (CLI)", "responsibilities": ["Consume structured notes data from the parser", "Analyze the link graph to compute backlinks for each note", "Output an enriched structured data file including backlink information"]}, {"id": "C25", "name": "Search Indexer (CLI)", "responsibilities": ["Consume structured notes data from the parser (or enriched data if desired)", "Generate a static client-side search index artifact (e.g., JSON files)"]}, {"id": "C26", "name": "Site Renderer (CLI)", "responsibilities": ["Consume enriched structured data to generate final HTML pages using templates", "Copy generated pages, search index artifacts, and other static assets to the output directory"]}], "interfaces": [{"id": "IF23", "from": "C23", "to": "C24", "contract": "On-disk structured data file (e.g., notes.json) containing parsed note content/metadata and extracted forward links."}, {"id": "IF24", "from": "C23", "to": "C25", "contract": "On-disk structured data file (e.g., notes.json) containing parsed note content/metadata and extracted forward links."}, {"id": "IF25", "from": "C24", "to": "C26", "contract": "On-disk enriched data file (e.g., enriched-notes.json) containing backlink information per note."}, {"id": "IF26", "from": "C25", "to": "C26", "contract": "On-disk search index artifact(s) (e.g., search-index.json and related files) to be copied/embedded into the final site output."}], "tradeoffs": {"pros": ["High modularity: each stage can be developed, tested, and replaced independently", "Easier to mix technologies across stages (e.g., parser in one language, renderer in another)", "Clear intermediate artifact(s) can aid debugging and reproducibility"], "cons": ["More complex build orchestration for the end-user compared to a single command", "I/O overhead from writing/reading intermediate files can reduce performance", "Intermediate schema/versioning must be maintained carefully across tools"]}, "risks": ["User experience may suffer if orchestration is cumbersome (multiple commands, ordering, cleanup)", "Intermediate JSON/schema changes require coordinated updates across multiple tools", "Disk usage can increase due to large intermediate artifacts on big note sets"]}], "chosen": {"option_id": "O1", "rationale": "The monolithic single-command CLI (O1) minimises upfront design overhead, avoids plugin-API or SSG-dependency risks, and delivers the fastest path to a working end-to-end prototype. All build stages run in-memory in a single process, simplifying debugging and deployment. Thin-slice milestones let each core goal (G1–G5) be validated incrementally. The trade-off is reduced long-term extensibility compared to O2 or O3, but this is acceptable given the project's scope and the explicit deferral of COULD requirements to post-MVP.", "high_level_dataflow": "User invokes CLI (C1) with input/output paths → C2 recursively discovers .md files, parses Markdown to AST, extracts frontmatter/tags/links → C3 builds forward-link graph and computes backlinks → C4 aggregates tags into per-tag indexes → C5 builds client-side search index → C6 renders HTML pages (injecting backlinks, tags, navigation) and writes static assets to output directory → C7 (client-side JS) loads search index in browser and provides search UI.", "key_design_decisions": ["DEC1", "DEC2", "DEC3", "DEC4", "DEC5", "DEC6", "DEC7"]}}, "milestones": [{"id": "M1", "name": "Core Ingestion & HTML Rendering", "deliverables": [{"id": "DL1", "text": "CLI entry point (C1) accepting input directory, output directory, and optional config path."}, {"id": "DL2", "text": "Markdown parser & metadata extractor (C2) with recursive .md discovery, frontmatter parsing, and Markdown-to-HTML rendering (raw HTML disabled, unsafe URL schemes blocked)."}, {"id": "DL3", "text": "HTML renderer/templating (C6) producing one static HTML page per note with stable deterministic URLs."}, {"id": "DL4", "text": "XSS security test suite covering K3 payloads (raw HTML, javascript: links)."}, {"id": "DL5", "text": "Acceptance tests AT1, AT2, AT3, AT4, AT13 passing."}], "exit_criteria": ["AT1 passes: all .md files recursively discovered, non-.md excluded.", "AT2 passes: output is static-only, no server runtime required.", "AT3 passes: Markdown formatting preserved in rendered HTML.", "AT4 passes: each note has a distinct, stable, deterministic URL.", "AT13 passes: build completes without errors on representative folder.", "XSS security tests pass (K3 mitigation verified).", "Blocking questions Q1 and Q2 resolved and documented before milestone work begins."], "depends_on": []}, {"id": "M2", "name": "Forward Links & Backlinks", "deliverables": [{"id": "DL6", "text": "Forward-link detection and rendering in C2/C6 using the resolved link syntax from Q1."}, {"id": "DL7", "text": "Graph engine (C3) computing backlinks from the corpus link graph."}, {"id": "DL8", "text": "Backlink section rendered on each note page via C6."}, {"id": "DL9", "text": "Fixture-based test dataset validating 100% backlink correctness (R21)."}, {"id": "DL10", "text": "Acceptance tests AT8, AT9 passing."}], "exit_criteria": ["AT8 passes: all internal forward links resolve and are clickable.", "AT9 passes: 100% of expected backlinks appear on target pages.", "Broken-link warnings emitted with source file/line (K1 mitigation).", "Backlink correctness validated against deterministic fixture dataset."], "depends_on": ["M1"]}, {"id": "M3", "name": "Tag Extraction & Navigation", "deliverables": [{"id": "DL11", "text": "Tag extraction logic in C2 supporting the resolved tag convention from Q2 (frontmatter and/or inline)."}, {"id": "DL12", "text": "Tag index builder (C4) producing per-tag note lists."}, {"id": "DL13", "text": "Per-tag navigation pages and tag index page rendered by C6."}, {"id": "DL14", "text": "Fixture-based test dataset validating 100% tag completeness (R20)."}, {"id": "DL15", "text": "Acceptance tests AT6, AT7 passing."}], "exit_criteria": ["AT6 passes: 100% of tagged notes appear under correct tag pages.", "AT7 passes: each tag has a navigable listing with working links.", "Tag completeness validated against deterministic fixture dataset."], "depends_on": ["M1"]}, {"id": "M4", "name": "Client-Side Search", "deliverables": [{"id": "DL16", "text": "Search index generator (C5) producing a client-side full-text index artifact at build time."}, {"id": "DL17", "text": "Client-side search UI (C7) loading the index and rendering results with title, snippet, and navigation."}, {"id": "DL18", "text": "Search quality benchmark against representative query set (R19)."}, {"id": "DL19", "text": "Search index size/performance benchmark for 100+ note dataset (K4)."}, {"id": "DL20", "text": "Acceptance tests AT5, AT12 passing."}], "exit_criteria": ["AT5 passes: search operates fully client-side without network.", "AT12 passes: ≥90% of representative queries return expected note in top 10.", "Search index size and query latency benchmarked and documented (K4)."], "depends_on": ["M1"]}, {"id": "M5", "name": "Polish & Optional Features", "deliverables": [{"id": "DL21", "text": "Clear error reporting for invalid Markdown, unresolvable links, and tag parsing failures with file paths and line numbers (R12)."}, {"id": "DL22", "text": "Cross-browser validation across Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge (R13)."}, {"id": "DL23", "text": "Watch mode for incremental regeneration (R25)."}, {"id": "DL24", "text": "Per-note table of contents generation (R24)."}, {"id": "DL25", "text": "Optional features scoped and implemented as approved: graph view (R26), theming (R27), advanced search (R28), nested tags (R29)."}, {"id": "DL26", "text": "Acceptance tests AT10, AT11 passing."}], "exit_criteria": ["AT10 passes: CLI build completes offline with input/output paths.", "AT11 passes: core features work without runtime errors in all target browsers.", "R12 error reporting verified on intentionally malformed inputs.", "Watch mode tested for edit/rename/delete scenarios (K14 mitigation).", "COULD features only implemented with explicit product approval (K20)."], "depends_on": ["M2", "M3", "M4"]}], "risk_register": [{"id": "K1", "severity": "high", "description": "Link/backlink resolution errors due to ambiguous or mixed internal link syntax (e.g., Markdown links vs. WikiLinks), causing broken navigation and incorrect backlink lists (blocking Q1).", "mitigation": {"text": "Resolve and document the supported internal link syntax (Q1). Implement a single canonical internal link model (normalized target IDs) with deterministic resolution rules. Add fixture-based tests for edge cases (relative paths, anchors, URL-encoding, renamed files). Emit build warnings for unresolved links including source locations.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K2", "severity": "high", "description": "Tag extraction inconsistency due to unspecified or mixed tag formats (frontmatter vs inline tags; nested tags), leading to missing/incorrect tag pages and filtering (blocking Q2).", "mitigation": {"text": "Resolve and document the tag specification (Q2). Implement a deterministic tag parser with explicit precedence rules and validation (report invalid tokens). Produce a build-time summary/tag inventory and add tests for the chosen formats (frontmatter, inline, optional nested).", "owner": "Product/Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K3", "severity": "critical", "description": "Client-side XSS or content injection vulnerabilities if Markdown/HTML is rendered unsafely (e.g., raw HTML passthrough, unsafe link protocols), compromising readers of the static site.", "mitigation": {"text": "Disable raw HTML by default (or sanitize it) in the renderer; block unsafe URL schemes (e.g., javascript:) and enforce safe attributes. Add security tests with known XSS payloads. If allowing trusted raw HTML, require explicit opt-in configuration and document the risk.", "owner": "Security/Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K4", "severity": "high", "description": "Client-side search index size/quality/performance may degrade at scale (large JS payload, slow queries, long build time), causing poor UX or crashes (related to Q3/SM7).", "mitigation": {"text": "Define expected scale and performance targets (Q3). Choose an index approach suitable for in-browser search; apply index-size controls (tokenization choices, compression, lazy loading/chunking where applicable). Add benchmark fixtures and CI performance budgets; validate search quality targets against representative queries.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K5", "severity": "medium", "description": "Slug/URL collisions (e.g., same filename in different folders, case-insensitive filesystems) cause pages to overwrite each other or links to resolve unpredictably.", "mitigation": {"text": "Define a deterministic slug strategy (include path segments and/or stable hashing). Detect collisions during build and fail with actionable errors unless an explicit override map is provided.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K6", "severity": "high", "description": "Non-deterministic builds (ordering differences, locale/time-dependent formatting, unpinned dependencies) produce noisy diffs and inconsistent site output across machines/CI.", "mitigation": {"text": "Enforce determinism: stable sorting of inputs, fixed locale/timezone handling, content-hash-based asset naming, and pinned dependency versions/lockfiles. Add a reproducibility check comparing outputs across two clean runs.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K7", "severity": "high", "description": "Markdown flavor/extension mismatch or unsupported/non-standard syntax yields rendering differences, broken formatting, or build failures relative to user expectations.", "mitigation": {"text": "Select and document a supported Markdown flavor and extensions (e.g., CommonMark baseline with explicit GFM extensions if supported). Add a conformance test pack with representative notes, robust error handling, and a strict mode that flags unsupported syntax.", "owner": "Product/Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K8", "severity": "medium", "description": "File encoding and Unicode handling issues (non-UTF8, BOM, mixed line endings) cause build failures or corrupted output text/search results.", "mitigation": {"text": "Assume UTF-8 by default but detect/handle BOM and common encodings where feasible. Normalize line endings internally. Emit clear diagnostics identifying offending files and provide a preflight validation command.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K9", "severity": "high", "description": "Path traversal or unintended file inclusion during ingestion (e.g., following symlinks, reading outside the intended directory) could leak local files into the generated site.", "mitigation": {"text": "Constrain ingestion to a declared root directory; default to not following symlinks; maintain an allowlist of file extensions. Reject paths escaping the root and generate an inclusion manifest for review.", "owner": "Security/Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K10", "severity": "medium", "description": "Backlink computation gaps for links with anchors, URL-encoded paths, or inconsistent normalization lead to partially missing backlink lists.", "mitigation": {"text": "Normalize link targets consistently (decode, resolve relative paths, standardize/strip anchors where appropriate) and test anchor links and encoded characters. Ensure link resolution uses the same canonicalization used for URL/slug generation.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K11", "severity": "medium", "description": "Broken offline/local viewing when opened via file:// due to browser restrictions (e.g., fetch/XHR blocked), especially impacting search and other JS features.", "mitigation": {"text": "Design search/runtime to work on static hosts; for local preview, provide guidance to run a simple local server. Optionally embed the index into a JS bundle to avoid runtime fetch, or detect file:// and show instructions.", "owner": "Engineering/Docs", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K12", "severity": "medium", "description": "Asset/link path resolution issues (broken relative paths, missing CSS/JS, incorrect base URL) can cause the site to work locally but fail when deployed under a subpath (e.g., GitHub Pages), and/or break nested-directory links/images.", "mitigation": {"text": "Support configurable basePath and generate links/assets relative to it. Establish a clear rule for resolving relative paths for notes and assets in nested directories. Add deployment-mode tests (non-root basePath) and nested-content fixtures with link/asset checks over the output.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K13", "severity": "medium", "description": "Excessive memory usage or slow build times on large repositories (including inefficient backlink generation) can cause build failures/timeouts in CI or on user machines.", "mitigation": {"text": "Profile CPU/memory usage; stream where possible; avoid loading all contents at once; optimize link-graph/backlink computation; implement caching/incremental indexing where feasible. Provide configurable limits (max file size, exclude globs) and a performance troubleshooting guide.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K14", "severity": "high", "description": "Incorrect incremental rebuild/watch behavior (if implemented) can lead to stale search index/backlinks after edits, renames, or deletes, confusing users.", "mitigation": {"text": "If watch mode is offered, implement a dependency graph so edits trigger recomputation of affected pages, backlinks, and search index. Provide a 'full rebuild' fallback and add tests for edit/rename/delete scenarios.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K15", "severity": "medium", "description": "Cross-browser compatibility and accessibility issues in generated HTML/CSS/JS (including search UI) may lead to runtime errors or reduced usability for some readers (SM6).", "mitigation": {"text": "Define target browsers and test across them. Adopt baseline accessibility guidelines for templates/components (semantic HTML, focus management, ARIA where needed). Add at least one automated audit step (e.g., Lighthouse/axe) plus manual spot checks.", "owner": "Engineering/Design", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K16", "severity": "medium", "description": "Overly permissive configuration or plugin/theme extensibility (if added) can introduce instability and make outputs hard to support/reproduce.", "mitigation": {"text": "Keep configuration surface minimal initially; validate configuration schemas; version configurations; gate plugin execution behind explicit allowlists and warnings. Provide a safe default preset and a compatibility policy.", "owner": "Product/Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K17", "severity": "medium", "description": "Information disclosure via generated artifacts (e.g., including private notes, embedding absolute filesystem paths in HTML/JS/search index).", "mitigation": {"text": "Support exclude patterns (globs) and a 'private' frontmatter flag. Ensure generated output never includes absolute source paths (use relative identifiers only). Emit a build manifest listing included sources for review.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K18", "severity": "high", "description": "Poorly managed third-party dependencies (e.g., Markdown parser, search indexer/SSG plugins) may introduce breaking changes or security vulnerabilities that destabilize the tool.", "mitigation": {"text": "Pin dependency versions and use a lockfile. Establish a dependency update/vetting process including automated vulnerability scanning and regression testing before upgrades.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K19", "severity": "medium", "description": "A complex installation process or system-specific dependencies for the CLI tool can create a high barrier to entry for users.", "mitigation": {"text": "Target a simple installation path (e.g., a single package manager). Document prerequisites clearly; minimize system-specific dependencies; consider producing distributable bundles where feasible.", "owner": "Engineering", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}, {"id": "K20", "severity": "low", "description": "Scope creep from undefined secondary features (e.g., graph views, themes) could divert resources from core goals and delay delivery.", "mitigation": {"text": "Prioritize core features for MVP; defer optional features until after MVP and track them as distinct work items with explicit approval before implementation.", "owner": "Product", "status": "planned"}, "acceptance": null}], "governance": {"failure_modes": [], "tool_policy": {"stage_policies": [{"stage": "Intake", "allowlisted_tools": ["artifact_read", "artifact_write"], "restrictions": [{"tool": "artifact_read", "rule": "provided_artifacts_only", "notes": "Read only the artifacts explicitly provided in inputs/artifact_refs; no external sources."}, {"tool": "artifact_write", "rule": "write_required_outputs_only", "allowed_artifacts": ["audit_spine", "intake_notes"], "notes": "Artifact writes limited to intake governance outputs for traceability."}, {"artifact_write": "canonical_allowed_only_for_declared_types", "notes": "Allow canonical audit-spine artifacts (run_manifest, event_log, stage_handoff)."}], "hitl_triggers": ["Blocking specification decisions are required but missing (Q1 internal link syntax; Q2 tag representation).", "Any request to expand scope beyond the static-site constraint."]}, {"stage": "Generate", "allowlisted_tools": ["artifact_read", "artifact_write"], "restrictions": [{"tool": "artifact_read", "rule": "provided_artifacts_only", "notes": "Do not use external web browsing or non-provided sources."}, {"tool": "artifact_write", "rule": "planning_only_no_execution_claims", "notes": "Drafting/planning only; do not execute code, access network, or claim runtime validation."}, {"tool": "artifact_write", "rule": "no_secrets_or_local_paths", "notes": "Do not include credentials/tokens or absolute filesystem paths in outputs."}], "hitl_triggers": ["Proposed solution requires server-side runtime for browsing/search/tags/backlinks (violates static constraint).", "Proposed Markdown rendering enables raw/unsanitized HTML or unsafe URL schemes without explicit mitigation."]}, {"stage": "Validate", "allowlisted_tools": ["artifact_read", "artifact_write"], "restrictions": [{"tool": "artifact_write", "rule": "validation_outputs_only", "allowed_artifacts": ["validation_notes", "risk_checks"], "notes": "Write only checklists/findings; do not introduce major scope changes during validation."}], "hitl_triggers": ["Security-sensitive findings (e.g., XSS risk) lack a concrete mitigation.", "Performance/scale targets remain undefined while performance-sensitive features are being committed."]}, {"stage": "Review", "allowlisted_tools": ["artifact_read", "artifact_write"], "restrictions": [{"tool": "artifact_write", "rule": "write_required_outputs_only", "allowed_artifacts": ["review_findings", "audit_spine"], "notes": "Review must be able to write findings and update the audit spine."}, {"tool": "artifact_write", "rule": "no_untracked_decisions", "notes": "Any decision affecting link/tag spec, security posture, or hosting assumptions must be logged in review_findings."}, {"artifact_write": "canonical_allowed_only_for_declared_types", "notes": "Allow findings-only canonical artifacts (review_findings.json)."}], "hitl_triggers": ["Any acceptance of high/critical risks without explicit signoff rationale.", "Any change to blocking questions (Q1/Q2) without stakeholder approval."]}, {"stage": "Judge", "allowlisted_tools": ["artifact_read", "artifact_write"], "restrictions": [{"tool": "artifact_write", "rule": "decision_record_only", "allowed_artifacts": ["governance_decision", "risk_acceptance_log"], "notes": "Record accept/mitigate decisions only; no new features introduced."}], "hitl_triggers": ["Any critical risk remains unmitigated.", "Unresolved blocking questions remain (Q1 or Q2)."]}, {"stage": "Freeze", "allowlisted_tools": ["artifact_read", "artifact_write"], "restrictions": [{"tool": "artifact_write", "rule": "freeze_outputs_only", "allowed_artifacts": ["frozen_risk_register", "frozen_tool_policy"], "notes": "Freeze produces locked governance artifacts; edits require a new run."}], "hitl_triggers": ["Any attempt to modify frozen artifacts without a formal change request."]}]}, "hitl_policy": {"when_to_interrupt": ["Blocking specification decisions are required (Q1 internal link syntax; Q2 tag representation) and are not provided.", "Any proposal that violates the static-site constraint (requires a server/database at runtime).", "Any security-sensitive behavior is proposed (raw HTML passthrough, unsanitized rendering, unsafe URL schemes) without an explicit mitigation and reviewer approval.", "Any high/critical risk is proposed for acceptance rather than mitigation, or is accepted without explicit signoff rationale.", "Any ingestion behavior could read outside the intended directory (symlinks/path traversal) without explicit user confirmation.", "On repeated failures to pass critical path test cases.", "Before making significant architectural changes or adding new major dependencies.", "When a generated solution deviates from the defined project capsule requirements.", "Upon detection of a high-severity security vulnerability in code or dependencies."], "approval_roles": ["Product Owner", "Product Manager", "Tech Lead", "Engineering Lead", "Security Reviewer", "Security Analyst"]}}, "decision_log": [{"id": "DEC1", "question": "Which architecture option to use?", "choice": "O1 — Monolithic single-command CLI", "rationale": "Minimises upfront design overhead and delivers the fastest path to a working end-to-end prototype. All stages run in-memory in a single process, simplifying debugging and deployment. Thin-slice milestones validate each goal incrementally.", "alternatives_considered": ["O2 — Custom plugin-based SSG core: higher extensibility but significant upfront API design cost and over-engineering risk for initial scope.", "O3 — Eleventy-based: reduces custom code but introduces SSG dependency constraints and upgrade risks.", "O4 — Multi-tool pipeline: high modularity but complex orchestration UX and intermediate schema maintenance."], "what_would_change_this_decision": ["Requirement for third-party theme/plugin ecosystem support.", "Need to support multiple search backends or renderers simultaneously.", "Scale exceeding thousands of notes where SSG incremental builds (O3) would provide significant performance advantage."], "evidence_pointers": [{"artifact_ref": "architecture_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "O1", "json_pointer": "/options/0", "note": "Monolithic CLI option definition", "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": null}, {"artifact_ref": "branch_set_v1", "entity_id": "B1", "json_pointer": "/branches/0", "note": "Branch B1 selects O1", "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": null}]}, {"id": "DEC2", "question": "What milestone strategy to follow?", "choice": "Thin-slice: each milestone delivers a shippable, testable increment covering a distinct core goal.", "rationale": "Thin slices allow early validation of each goal (G1–G5) against its acceptance tests before proceeding, reducing integration risk and enabling early feedback.", "alternatives_considered": ["Layer-cake: build all backend components first, then UI — delays end-to-end validation.", "Big-bang: single milestone with all features — high integration risk and late feedback."], "what_would_change_this_decision": ["Strong coupling between features that prevents independent slicing.", "Stakeholder preference for a single comprehensive delivery."], "evidence_pointers": [{"artifact_ref": "branch_set_v1", "entity_id": "B1", "json_pointer": "/branches/0/milestone_strategy", "note": "Thin-slice strategy defined in branch", "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": null}]}, {"id": "DEC3", "question": "When to resolve blocking questions Q1 (link syntax) and Q2 (tag format)?", "choice": "Resolve both before any coding begins (pre-M1 gate).", "rationale": "Q1 and Q2 are blocking; link syntax affects C2, C3, and C6, while tag format affects C2 and C4. Deferring them would cause rework across multiple components. Alignment warnings AL-001 and AL-002 flag these as blockers.", "alternatives_considered": ["Defer Q1 to M2 and Q2 to M3 — risks rework in M1 parser if conventions change.", "Support all formats from the start — increases complexity and testing surface withou