y in C2; reject symlinks by default; reject paths escaping the root.", "rationale": "K9 is high severity. Following symlinks or allowing path escape could leak local files into the generated site. Rejecting symlinks is the safe default.", "alternatives_considered": ["Follow symlinks with user confirmation — adds complexity and residual risk.", "No restriction — unacceptable given high severity."], "what_would_change_this_decision": ["User workflow requires symlinked note directories and explicitly opts in."], "evidence_pointers": [{"artifact_ref": "risk_gov_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "K9", "json_pointer": "/risk_register/8", "note": "Path traversal risk", "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": null}]}, {"id": "DEC6", "question": "When to address search index scalability (K4)?", "choice": "Defer concrete benchmarking to M4 with a defined performance budget step; apply basic index-size controls (stemming, stop words) from the start.", "rationale": "Search is delivered in M4. Benchmarking earlier would be premature since the index generator (C5) is not built until M4. Basic controls are low-cost to include from the start.", "alternatives_considered": ["Benchmark in M1 — premature, no search component exists yet.", "Ignore until post-MVP — unacceptable given high severity of K4."], "what_would_change_this_decision": ["User confirms a very large corpus (10k+ notes) requiring chunked/sharded indexing from the start.", "Performance targets defined earlier via Q3 resolution."], "evidence_pointers": [{"artifact_ref": "risk_gov_canonical_v1", "entity_id": "K4", "json_pointer": "/risk_register/3", "note": "Search index scale risk", "candidate_id": null, "artifact_id": null, "quote": null}]}, {"id": "DEC7", "question": "How to handle COULD-priority features (R26–R29)?", "choice": "Explicitly defer to post-M5; only implement with product approval to avoid scope creep (K20).", "rationale": "K20 identifies scope creep risk. COULD features are not required for core go